Hooks for syncing with the browser's own account and relay, in place of Google's sign-in and FCM
(//browser_core/hooks.h, set in //browser_core/sync.cc).

SyncAuthManager takes the account to sync and its access tokens from the core when it sets
g_browser_core_sync_account and g_browser_core_sync_token: the account, already marked as not
managed, since Google's managed-status finder would wait for an account it doesn't know, and each
token, answered later through the same AccessTokenFetched a Google token takes, so expiry and the
server's 401 ask the core again. g_browser_core_sync_account_watch gives the core the call that
IdentityManager's events would make, for when the user signs in or out.
SyncInvalidationsServiceFactory takes the core's service, which hears from the relay, when it sets
g_browser_core_sync_invalidations.
SyncServiceImpl gives the engine the core's server when it sets g_browser_core_sync_url, read as
each engine starts, so a server the user names takes effect at their next sign-in, without a
restart, where --sync-url is read once.

